member.remarks:
When several columns have the same name, the first one wins; 
finds the others. Without a header ( is ), no name
is found.

member.summary:
The 0-based index of the column, used instead of the header; needed when the input has no header.
-1 (the default) finds the column by name. For a collection member, the first of its columns (see
).

Whether the column may be missing from the header. A missing optional member keeps its default value;
a missing required one makes  throw. Constructor parameters with a
default value are always optional.

Reads records of type  from the columns of one reader's header. The CsvHelper source
generator writes one for each  type; 
creates it.

member.param:
The value. It is quoted when it contains the separator, a quote, CR or LF (or always, with
), or escaped or padded as  says; invalid
UTF-16 is replaced with U+FFFD.

The value. It is quoted when it contains the separator, a quote, CR or LF (or always, with
), or escaped or padded as  says; invalid
UTF-16 is replaced with U+FFFD.

member.summary:
The strings of one column: an open addressing table keyed by the bytes of the value. Lookups take no
lock (an entry is published by writing its  last and never changes afterwards;
growing replaces the table); adding a value locks.
